    <h1 style="font-size: 24pt;">TITLE XV</h1>
    <h2 style="font-size: 20pt;">EDUCATION</h2>
    <h3 style="font-size: 16pt;">CHAPTER 187-A</h3>
    <h3 style="font-size: 16pt;">STATE COLLEGE AND UNIVERSITY SYSTEM</h3>
    <h3 style="font-size: 16pt;">University System</h3>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">Section 187-A:2</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">187-A:2 Components of the University System. – The university system of New Hampshire shall consist of the university of New Hampshire (including the New Hampshire college of agriculture and the mechanic arts and its other colleges, schools and divisions), the Plymouth state university, the Keene state college, and the Granite state college.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 30px;">Source. 1981, 331:1. 1985, 140:1. 1993, 109:1. eff. July 1, 1993. 2003, 159:1. Aug. 16, 2003. 2005, 13:1. eff. May 9, 2005.</p>
  </div>
